{
  "name": "Day13A:  Agent Patterns - Routing and Specialist Agents LOCKED",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Objective\n**Day 13**\nLearning Objectives:\n- Why one large agent is difficult to maintain\n- Separation of concerns\n- Router pattern\n- Specialist agents\n- Agent delegation\n- Shared memory\n- Extensible agent architectures\n\n### Highlights\n- multiple Agents can share the same LLM.\n- The Context is owned by the agent (not the LLM), and the agent uses memory to maintain the state (conversation history)\n- The agents can use the same (shared) memory.\n\n#[Guide](https://docs.n8n.io/workflows/components/sticky-notes/)",
        "height": 640,
        "width": 496
      },
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
